# Charts — manual only

Chart tabs on any ticker’s Google Sheet must not be created, edited, or repointed by agents or Python scripts (including `updateChartSpec`, series range changes, axis/scale settings, colors, or legend).

For **OPEN**, that means **Homes Charts** and **Money Charts**. Other tickers may use different chart tab names — the same ban applies.

The Sheets API does not preserve full chart styling (colors, log scale, custom axes, etc.). Automated chart edits have repeatedly broken these tabs.

## Allowed

- Read chart metadata for debugging or answering questions
- Edit financials data and formulas (charts may drift if rows are inserted — tell the user to fix chart series manually in the UI)

## Not allowed without explicit user request

- `updateChartSpec` or any batch update touching chart objects
- New tabs or scripts whose purpose is to repoint or rebuild charts
- Running `scripts/restore_charts.py` (emergency rollback only; user must ask)

## When row layout changes

After inserting or deleting rows on Weekly / Quarterly Financials (or the equivalent data tabs for that ticker):

1. Run the formula restore flow (`validate_model_formulas.py --ticker …`, `restore_weekly_model_formulas.py --ticker …`, etc.)
2. **Tell the user** to verify and adjust chart series manually in the Google Sheets UI if lines look wrong — do not fix charts yourself
